From 5603990c336a5c0b6a77558712aaf52d7eb63044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:14:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native DB dump tool and Rust/native parity harness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tools/chronik_native_dump.cpp (chronik-native-dump) prints a schema v13
Chronik index, Rust- or native-built, as sorted
"table<TAB>key_hex<TAB>value_hex" lines with dup values expanded.

contrib/chronik-parity (design §8.3) runs two Chronik builds on one
deterministic regtest chain: a separate miner feeds identical blocks
and transactions to both (P2PKH/P2SH/P2PK/bare/other scripts, OP_RETURN
LOKAD, SLP fungible/NFT1/mint vault and ALP incl. invalid and burn
cases, mempool conflicts, reorgs, invalidate/reconsider, broadcasts).
At checkpoints it compares an HTTP corpus over every route (status,
headers, raw bytes and parsed protobuf; pagination edges, malformed
params, content types, body limits, batch limits), WebSocket sessions
for every subscription type, and optionally the DB dumps. Validated
Rust-vs-Rust (zero differences over 85k requests and 469 sessions on a
400-block run) and against a negative control.

Tier: eCash

